caption: Limitations, Power, and Maintenance — Power-cell rules that matter in play
technology-rule: power-cell-rules-that-matter-in-play

| Rule | Practical Effect |
| --- | --- |
| Rechargeable is standard | Ordinary cells can be recharged and have indefinite shelf life when unused. |
| Non-rechargeable cells | Last twice as long or provide twice as many shots, but cannot be recharged. |
| Redundant cells | Life-support and flight systems often use two or more cells so one can take over without interruption. |
| Emergency substitution | Ten cells of one size replace one cell of the next larger size; jury-rigging normally calls for Electrician and time. |
| Cross-cultural incompatibility | Different voltages, connectors, or mana standards may require Electrician, Armoury, or a source-specific skill. |

Rules basis: GURPS Ultra-Tech, pp. 18-22 and 207-208. Treat the listed durations as equipment benchmarks, not as a universal conversion from cell size to hours.
